title: Buggs
tags:
---
Joss: Hmm, what's this? A little stall in the middle of nowhere?

Bunny: Ah, welcome, traveler! You've found Buggs' Burrow of Baubles! I'm Buggs, provider of the finest jewelry you'll find this side of the forest.

Joss: You're...a bunny. Selling jewelry?

Bunny: Indeed! Who better to craft treasures than someone with nimble paws and an eye for shiny things?

Joss: Fair point. What kind of jewelry are we talking about here?

Bunny: Oh, only the most exquisite! Rings, necklaces, and earrings, all made from the finest forest gems and enchanted silver. Interested? 

    -> "Sure, show me what you've got."
            Bunny: (grinning and pulling out a sparkling tray) Excellent choice! Here, we have a moonstone pendant that glows under starlight, a ring that can grant you fleeting luck, and these earrings—crafted from dragonfly wings. Lovely, aren’t they?

            Joss: (examining the pieces) These are beautiful. How much?

            Bunny: (tapping their chin) For you, let's say... one golden acorn or two shiny river pebbles. 

            -> "Deal! I’ll take the moonstone pendant."
                Bunny: (happily hopping) Wonderful choice! Here you go. Handle it with care—moonstones are known to bond with their owners.

                Joss: (taking the pendant) Thanks, Buggs. You’ve got a talent for this, you know.

                Bunny: (beaming) Why thank you, traveler! Come back anytime. And if you find any rare gems or shiny things on your journeys, think of me!

                Joss: Will do. Take care, Buggs. (puts on the pendant and walks away, the moonstone faintly glowing under the sunlight)

                End
            -> "I don’t have any of that. How about this instead?" [Player offers item]
                Bunny: (inspecting the offered item) Hmm, let me see... Oh, this is lovely! I’ll gladly trade for this.

                Joss: (handing over the item) Deal. I’ve got a good feeling about this moonstone pendant.

                Bunny: You’ve got a sharp eye! Wear it well, traveler. And if you find more treasures, you know where to find me!

                Joss: (smiling) Thanks, Buggs. Until next time.

                End
    -> "Jewelry isn't really my thing."
            Bunny: (tilting their head) Not a fan of shiny things? That’s rare. But no worries, perhaps you’d be more interested in a charm bracelet for luck or a brooch that keeps bad dreams away?

            Joss: (hesitant) I guess I could take a look...

            -> "Show me the charm bracelet." 
                Bunny: (placing the charm bracelet on the counter) This one’s special. Each charm tells a story, and the bracelet itself is said to bring good fortune.

                Joss: (examining it) It’s beautiful. How much?

                Bunny: (smiling warmly) For you, just a shiny river pebble.

                Joss: (grinning) Sold. Here you go. Thanks, Bijou.

                Bunny: My pleasure! May it bring you all the luck you need. And remember, come back anytime!

                Joss: I will. See you around, Buggs.

                End
            -> "No thanks. I’ll pass."
                Bunny: (nodding politely) Fair enough, traveler. Not everyone is drawn to the shimmer of baubles. But if you ever change your mind, Bijou’s Burrow of Baubles will always be here.

                Joss: (shrugging) Maybe next time. Take care, Buggs.

                Bunny: (waving a paw) Safe travels!

                End
    ===
